HOW TO CREATE A NEW REPOSITORY?? 
Use any version control provider like GitHub, GitLab, Bitbucket, etc. 
Create an account and create a repo based on the requirement. If it is for collaboration and an internal project you don't wanna reveal,
then go ahead with private mode. Otherwise, like if you wanna display your work better, go with creating public mode.


HOW DO THEY WORK?? 
It is used for collaboration, code maintenance, and virtual code storage - write code, 
download wherever you want for deploying, developing, etc.

WHERE TO PUSH THEM?? 
From your physical system repo to a remote repo. You should have the Git Bash tool to commit the latest code, 
which is an open-source tool and supports all OS's like Windows, Ubuntu, Linux, Mac. Steps to update your code to the repo.
1. git add -A or -a or . 
    else specific folder or file path
2. git commit -m 'here you provide message. which should describe your work update/ changes you have made with short description with ticket number'
3. git push (or) git push origin <branch name>

HOW TO EDIT THEM??
You mean code. To edit code, you can do the same process. But before editing, you should 'git pull origin <branch name> to get updated code
Before you start the task, do git pull origin < branch name> to avoid merge conflicts.

WHAT IS GIT BASH?? 
It is used to run Git and Unix-like commands. Like clone, push, pull, and resolve merge conflicts, maintain branches, 
cherry-picking, etc in your local system repo.

HOW TO WORK WITH COMMAND PROMPTS CMD'S??
For real-time, it is better to use GitBash for color lints. Try to avoid PowerShell or cmd
